item.text:
Severity class: isolated major political violence plus post-event institutional failure and remediation, not systematic state terror. The record supports a broadly protective open-society baseline in 2022, with the Abe assassination as the main domestic-safety shock and Kishida’s response centered on condemnation, policing review, and victim relief.

**Reused evidence**
REUSE_JSON: {"evidence_ids":["E0001"],"lenses":["3B.10"]}

**New evidence**
- [Press Conference by the Prime Minister on the Attack Perpetrated against Former Prime Minister ABE Shinzo](https://japan.kantei.go.jp/101_kishida/statement/202207/_00002.html) - Kishida condemned the shooting as unforgivable and said the government would take every possible measure.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Press Conference by the Prime Minister on the Attack Perpetrated against Former Prime Minister ABE Shinzo","publisher":"Prime Minister's Office of Japan","publication_date":"2022-07-08","url":"https://japan.kantei.go.jp/101_kishida/statement/202207/_00002.html","claim":"Kishida condemned Abe's shooting as an unforgivable and despicable act during an election campaign and said the government would take every possible measure.","locator":"opening remarks, first response block","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct PMO transcript from the day of the attack.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Immediate response to a major domestic political killing in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct first-person response by Kishida as prime minister.","contrary_evidence":["The attack exposed a serious VIP-security failure that Kishida inherited rather than caused."],"lenses":["3B.9","3B.10"]}

- [トピックスI　要人警護の強化に係る警察の取組](https://www.npa.go.jp/hakusyo/r05/honbun/html/zt100000.html) - The National Police Agency said it could not protect Abe’s life, created a verification team, and issued a report on August 25, 2022.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"トピックスI　要人警護の強化に係る警察の取組","publisher":"National Police Agency of Japan","publication_date":"2023-?","url":"https://www.npa.go.jp/hakusyo/r05/honbun/html/zt100000.html","claim":"The National Police Agency said it could not protect Abe's life, created a verification and review team, and produced a report on August 25, 2022 to improve VIP protection.","locator":"opening paragraphs on the Abe shooting and the August 25 report","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary police-white-paper material describing the institution's own review of the 2022 failure.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Retrospective official account of 2022 domestic-security failure and remedy.","ruler_attribution":"Institutional response under Kishida's cabinet, not a private act by Kishida alone.","contrary_evidence":["This is remedial action after failure, not proof of prior effective protection."],"lenses":["3B.2","3B.4","3B.9","3B.10"]}

- [Japan police chief to resign over Abe shooting, citing 'fresh start'](https://uk.news.yahoo.com/japan-police-chief-wants-resign-053556754.html) - Reuters reported the NPA chief resigned to take responsibility and said the security plan needed a fresh start.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Japan police chief to resign over Abe shooting, citing 'fresh start'","publisher":"Reuters","publication_date":"2022-08-25","url":"https://uk.news.yahoo.com/japan-police-chief-wants-resign-053556754.html","claim":"The National Police Agency chief said he would resign to take responsibility for Abe's murder and described the need for a fresh start and a new security plan.","locator":"lead paragraphs and quoted resignation explanation","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters is strong independent monitoring; this is a republished wire report.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 follow-up to the assassination.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but explicit to the Kishida-led police apparatus.","contrary_evidence":["The report reflects failure and correction rather than effective prevention."],"lenses":["3B.2","3B.4","3B.10"]}

- [Press Conference by Prime Minster Kishida](https://japan.kantei.go.jp/101_kishida/statement/202208/_00007.html) - Kishida said the National Public Safety Commission chair must verify the Abe killing and rebuild security arrangements.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Press Conference by Prime Minster Kishida","publisher":"Prime Minister's Office of Japan","publication_date":"2022-08-10","url":"https://japan.kantei.go.jp/101_kishida/statement/202208/_00007.html","claim":"Kishida said the new chair of the National Public Safety Commission must thoroughly verify the killing of former Prime Minister Abe and rebuild security arrangements.","locator":"cabinet-reshuffle remarks on public safety","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct PMO transcript of Kishida's cabinet-reshuffle instructions.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 institutional response to the assassination shock.","ruler_attribution":"Direct first-person instruction by Kishida as prime minister.","contrary_evidence":["It follows a major failure rather than demonstrating a preexisting protective record."],"lenses":["3B.4","3B.9","3B.10"]}

- [Press Conference by Prime Minster Kishida](https://japan.kantei.go.jp/101_kishida/statement/202208/_00031.html) - Kishida said religious groups must obey the law and ordered stronger victim-support and consultation measures for fraud-like practices.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Press Conference by Prime Minster Kishida","publisher":"Prime Minister's Office of Japan","publication_date":"2022-08-31","url":"https://japan.kantei.go.jp/101_kishida/statement/202208/_00031.html","claim":"Kishida instructed that religious groups must obey laws and ordinances and that the government should strengthen consultation and victim-support measures for wrongful business practices and related harm.","locator":"instructions on two points in the opening statement","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct PMO transcript with explicit instructions to his cabinet and ministries.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 response to the Unification Church crisis.","ruler_attribution":"Direct first-person instruction by Kishida as prime minister.","contrary_evidence":["The statement is remedial and does not erase the underlying scandal."],"lenses":["3B.4","3B.7","3B.10"]}

- [Japan PM defends decision on state funeral for Abe](https://www.euronews.com/2022/09/09/japan-politics-unification-church-kishida) - Kishida accepted that his explanation was insufficient while the funeral drew widespread public opposition.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Japan PM defends decision on state funeral for Abe","publisher":"Reuters via Euronews","publication_date":"2022-09-09","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/09/09/japan-politics-unification-church-kishida","claim":"Kishida accepted criticism that his explanation for the state funeral was insufficient while the funeral drew widespread public opposition.","locator":"report body and quoted parliamentary response","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire report republished by Euronews; useful for contemporaneous reaction and protest climate.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 domestic political crisis response.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributed to Kishida's handling of the funeral decision.","contrary_evidence":["Public backlash is evidence of controversy, not of state repression by Kishida."],"lenses":["3B.8","3B.9","3B.10"]}

- [Japan prepares for slain PM Shinzo Abe's state funeral](https://reuters.screenocean.com/record/1690504) - Reuters reported police patrols and protest preparations around the funeral, with the event a flashpoint for public anger.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Japan prepares for slain PM Shinzo Abe's state funeral","publisher":"Reuters Archive Licensing / Screenocean","publication_date":"2022-09-26","url":"https://reuters.screenocean.com/record/1690504","claim":"Reuters reported that police officers were on patrol while protesters and local residents expressed opposition around Abe's state funeral, which had become a flashpoint for public anger.","locator":"story text summary of preparations and public reaction","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters text summary of contemporaneous reporting; direct but republished in archive form.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct pre-funeral 2022 public-dissent episode.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to the Kishida government decision to hold the funeral.","contrary_evidence":["The report shows protest tolerated and policed, not crushed."],"lenses":["3B.8","3B.9"]}

- [Policy Speech by Prime Minister KISHIDA Fumio to the 210th Session of the Diet](https://japan.kantei.go.jp/101_kishida/statement/202210/_00003.html) - Kishida said he was listening to public voices on the former Unification Church and would build consultation services and legal support to prevent recurrence.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Policy Speech by Prime Minister KISHIDA Fumio to the 210th Session of the Diet","publisher":"Prime Minister's Office of Japan","publication_date":"2022-10-03","url":"https://japan.kantei.go.jp/101_kishida/statement/202210/_00003.html","claim":"Kishida said he was listening steadfastly to public voices on relationships with the former Unification Church and would set up consultation services and legal support to provide relief and prevent recurrence.","locator":"speech section on the former Unification Church and relief measures","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct PMO transcript of a major Diet policy speech.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 legislative and administrative response.","ruler_attribution":"Direct first-person policy commitment by Kishida as prime minister.","contrary_evidence":["This is a remedial response after the crisis, not evidence of prior prevention."],"lenses":["3B.4","3B.6","3B.7","3B.10"]}

- [Japan PM orders probe into Unification Church links to ruling party members](https://www.investing.com/news/world-news/japan-pm-orders-probe-into-unification-church-links-to-ruling-party-members-2913437) - Reuters reported Kishida ordered an investigation into the church after the assassination revealed ties to ruling-party lawmakers.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Japan PM orders probe into Unification Church links to ruling party members","publisher":"Reuters","publication_date":"2022-10-17","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/world-news/japan-pm-orders-probe-into-unification-church-links-to-ruling-party-members-2913437","claim":"Kishida ordered an investigation into the Unification Church after Abe's assassination revealed close ties between the church and ruling party lawmakers.","locator":"lead paragraph","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters is strong independent monitoring; this is a republished wire report.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 accountability response.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributed to Kishida's order as prime minister.","contrary_evidence":["The probe is accountability after harm, not a preventive safety success in itself."],"lenses":["3B.4","3B.7","3B.10"]}

- [Japan govt begins Unification Church probe amid anger over ties with ruling party](https://www.marketscreener.com/news/latest/Japan-govt-begins-Unification-Church-probe-amid-anger-over-ties-with-ruling-party-42379875/) - Reuters reported the government launched a probe that could strip the church of legal status and tax exemptions.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Japan govt begins Unification Church probe amid anger over ties with ruling party","publisher":"Reuters","publication_date":"2022-11-21","url":"https://www.marketscreener.com/news/latest/Japan-govt-begins-Unification-Church-probe-amid-anger-over-ties-with-ruling-party-42379875/","claim":"The Japanese government launched a probe into the Unification Church that could strip the group of legal status and tax exemptions.","locator":"lead paragraph and subsequent explanation of the probe","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters is strong independent monitoring; this is a republished wire report.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct late-2022 accountability action.","ruler_attribution":"Government action under Kishida's administration.","contrary_evidence":["This remains an investigative and legal step, not proof of improved protection yet."],"lenses":["3B.4","3B.7","3B.10"]}

- [Press Conference by Prime Minister Kishida](https://japan.kantei.go.jp/101_kishida/statement/202212/_00004.html) - Kishida said he personally met victims, ordered a new law, and built a government support structure to help them use it.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Press Conference by Prime Minister Kishida","publisher":"Prime Minister's Office of Japan","publication_date":"2022-12-10","url":"https://japan.kantei.go.jp/101_kishida/statement/202212/_00004.html","claim":"Kishida said he met directly with people harmed by the former Unification Church, ordered a new law within constitutional limits, and set up a government-wide support system with the Japan Legal Support Center and other bodies.","locator":"opening statement on the relief law and follow-up support","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct PMO transcript with explicit account of legislative and administrative action.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct end-of-year 2022 remedy and accountability action.","ruler_attribution":"Direct first-person leadership claim by Kishida as prime minister.","contrary_evidence":["Relief legislation mitigates harm but does not undo the harm already done."],"lenses":["3B.4","3B.7","3B.10"]}

- [2022 Country Report on Human Rights Practices: Japan](https://www.ecoi.net/en/document/2089494.html) - The State Department said there were no arbitrary killings, disappearances, or credible torture by officials, and that civilians authorities maintained effective control.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"2022 Country Report on Human Rights Practices: Japan","publisher":"United States Department of State","publication_date":"2023","url":"https://www.ecoi.net/en/document/2089494.html","claim":"The State Department reported no arbitrary or unlawful killings, no disappearances, no credible torture by officials, and effective civilian control over the security forces.","locator":"Executive Summary and Section 1a-1c","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Government human-rights report summarizing the 2022 record with direct, structured findings.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Retrospective report on the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"National baseline rather than a single Kishida action, but relevant to end-state safety and attribution limits.","contrary_evidence":["The same report notes some abuses and discrimination issues affecting minorities, migrants, and Indigenous people."],"lenses":["3B.1","3B.2","3B.10"]}

- [2022 Country Report on Human Rights Practices: Japan](https://www.ecoi.net/en/document/2089494.html) - The State Department said freedom of assembly and association was generally respected and there were no restrictions on speaking out about LGBTQI+ matters.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"2022 Country Report on Human Rights Practices: Japan","publisher":"United States Department of State","publication_date":"2023","url":"https://www.ecoi.net/en/document/2089494.html","claim":"The State Department reported that the constitution provides for freedom of assembly and association, the government generally respected those rights, and there were no restrictions on speaking out about LGBTQI+ matters.","locator":"Section 2b-2c and the LGBTQI+ subsection","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Structured government report on the 2022 domestic civil-liberties environment.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Retrospective report on the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Country baseline rather than direct Kishida action, but relevant to protest and vulnerable-group protection.","contrary_evidence":["The report still notes discrimination and specific social harms affecting some groups."],"lenses":["3B.7","3B.8"]}

- [2022 Country Report on Human Rights Practices: Japan](https://www.ecoi.net/en/document/2089494.html) - The report noted credible violence or threats targeting persons with disabilities, minority groups, and Indigenous peoples.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"2022 Country Report on Human Rights Practices: Japan","publisher":"United States Department of State","publication_date":"2023","url":"https://www.ecoi.net/en/document/2089494.html","claim":"The State Department identified credible violence or threats of violence targeting persons with disabilities, national or racial or ethnic minorities, and Indigenous peoples as significant human-rights issues.","locator":"Executive Summary, significant human-rights issues paragraph","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Same structured country report, but this is a distinct substantive claim about residual domestic harms.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Retrospective report on the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Country-level harm not clearly attributable to Kishida personally, but material for end-state safety.","contrary_evidence":["The report does not indicate systematic state terror or ruler-directed mass repression."],"lenses":["3B.7","3B.10"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
- I considered roughly 30 documents across PMO transcripts, Diet-related releases, the National Police Agency, Reuters text/mirror copies, the State Department country report, and human-rights background material.
- I retained 13 source-claim units from 12 distinct URLs because they were the most direct 2022 Kishida-attributed records on domestic violence prevention, police accountability, protest handling, and the Unification Church fallout.
- I rejected duplicate mirror pages of the same Reuters report when the wire text was already captured once.
- I rejected later retrospective pages from 2023-2026 unless they were only needed to locate a 2022 record; they were not treated as evidence for 2022 conduct.
- I rejected broad democracy summaries that repeated the same “Japan is generally open” point without adding ruler-attributed 2022 domestic-safety detail.
- I rejected foreign-policy and nuclear-security documents that belonged to Chapters 1B or 2B rather than domestic safety.
- I did not re-fetch the local structured priors you already supplied, and I did not use the client matrix.

**Remaining gaps**
- There is no evidence of Kishida personally inciting domestic hatred or violence in 2022; that absence is meaningful, but it is still absence-based rather than a positive proof.
- The main unresolved issue is how much Kishida himself drove the police and intelligence reforms versus simply endorsing institutional correction after the assassination.
- The record on vulnerable-group protection is mostly country-level and remedial, not a direct account of a Kishida-led domestic safety campaign.
- More searching would probably not change the core picture much unless you want a deeper dive on police reform minutes, Diet oversight hearings, or Japanese-language reporting on protest policing and religious-fraud victim relief.
